 We work backwards from $a_{13} = 2016$. Since $a_{11}, a_{12}, a_{13}$ form a geometric sequence, we can write $a_{13} = (a_{11})(a_{12})^2$. Since $a_{12}, a_{13}, a_{14}$ form an arithmetic sequence, we can write $a_{14} - a_{13} = a_{13} - a_{12}$, or $a_{14} = 2a_{13} - a_{12}$. We now have a system of equations to solve:
\begin{align*}
