Since $a_1, a_2, \dots, a_{14}$ are positive integers, we know that $a_{12}$ is a factor of $2016 = 2^{5} \cdot 3 \cdot 67$. Therefore, $a_{12}$ is at least $2^4 = 16$ (since it is positive and an integer). Similarly, $a_{11} \le a_{12}$ and $a_{14} \le 2a_{13}$, so $a_{11}$ is at most $a_{12}$ and $a_{14}$ is at most $4032$. Checking factors of $2016$ in the range $16 \le a_{12} \le 4032$, we find that $a_{12} = 16$ (the only such value that makes $a_{11}$ and $a_{14}$ positive integers). Substituting into our equations gives $a_{11} = 126$ and $a_{14} = 4032$.

Now we work with $a_9, a_{10}, a_{11}, a_{12}, a_{13}$. Since $a_{11}, a_{12}, a_{13}$ form a geometric sequence, $a_{13} = (a_{11})(a_{12})^2$, or $2016 = 126a_{12}^2$. Therefore $a_{12} = 4$, and we can find $a_{11} = 6$ and $a_{13} = 336$.

Finally, $a_7, a_8, a_9, a_{10}, a_{11}, a_{12}, a_{13}$ form part of an arithmetic sequence, so $a_9 = a_{11} - 2(a_{13} - a_{12}) = 6 - 2(336 - 4) = -658$. Therefore, $a_{10} = a_9 + (a_{12} - a_9) = -658 + (4 - (-658)) = 1320$. Since $a_8, a_9, a_{10}$ form an arithmetic sequence, $a_8 = a_9 - (a_{10} - a_9) = -658 - (1320 - (-658)) = -2646$. Similarly, $a_6, a_7, a_8$ form an arithmetic sequence, so $a_7 = a_6 + (a_8 - a_7)$, and $a_6 = 2a_7 - a_8 = 2(-2646) - (-658) = -5634$.

