The base of each right triangle is half the length of the base of the isosceles triangle, which is 6/2 = 3 units. The height of each right triangle is the same as the height of the isosceles triangle, which is the length of the side of the isosceles triangle that is not the base. So, the height of each right triangle is 5 units.

