The cross product of $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} c \\ d \end{pmatrix}$ is $ad - bc$, so $ad - bc = 18$, and the cross product of $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} -d \\ c \end{pmatrix}$ is $ab + cd$, so $ab + cd = 72$.
We want to minimize $a + b + c + d$, so we should minimize the values of $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$.
