 First, let's simplify each individual term inside the square root. 

The term $\sqrt{80}$ can be simplified as follows:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{80} &= \sqrt{16 \times 5} \\
&= \sqrt{16} \times \sqrt{5} \\
&= 4\sqrt{5}.
\end{align*}

Similarly, the term $\sqrt{845}$ can be simplified as follows:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{845} &= \sqrt{169 \times 5} \\
&= \sqrt{169} \times \sqrt{5} \\
&= 13\sqrt{5}.
\end{align*}

The term $\sqrt{45}$ can be simplified as follows:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{45} &= \sqrt{9 \times 5} \\
&= \sqrt{9} \times \sqrt{5} \\
&= 3\sqrt{5}.
\end{align*}

Now we substitute these simplified terms back into the original expression:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{5}{\sqrt{80}}+\dfrac{\sqrt{845}}{9}+\sqrt{45}}{\sqrt5}} &= \sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{5}{4\sqrt{5}}+\dfrac{13\sqrt{5}}{9}+3\sqrt{5}}{\sqrt5}} \\
&= \sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{5}{4\sqrt{5}}+\dfrac{13\sqrt{5}}{9}+\dfrac{27\sqrt{5}}{9}}{\sqrt5}} \\
&= \sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{5+13\sqrt{5}+27\sqrt{5}}{4\sqrt{5}}}{\sqrt5}}.
\end{align*}

Next, we simplify the numerator in the fraction:
\begin{align*}
5+13\sqrt{5}+27\sqrt{5} &= 5+40\sqrt{5} \\
&= 5(1+8\sqrt{5}).
\end{align*}

Substitute this back into the expression:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{5+13\sqrt{5}+27\sqrt{5}}{4\sqrt{5}}}{\sqrt5}} &= \sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{5(1+8\sqrt{5})}{4\sqrt{5}}}{\sqrt5}}.
\end{align*}

Simplify the denominator:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{5} \times \sqrt{4\sqrt{5}} &= \sqrt{20} \\
&= \sqrt{4 \times 5} \\
&= 2\sqrt{5}.
\end{align*}

Substitute this back into the expression:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{5(1+8\sqrt{5})}{4\sqrt{5}}}{\sqrt5}} &= \sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{5(1+8\sqrt{5})}{2\sqrt{5}}}{\sqrt5}}.
\end{align*}

Cancel out the common $\sqrt{5}$ in the numerator and denominator:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{5(1+8\sqrt{5})}{2\sqrt{5}}}{\sqrt5}} &= \sqrt{\dfrac{5(1+8\sqrt{5})}{2\sqrt{5}} \times \dfrac{1}{\sqrt{5}}} \\
&= \sqrt{\dfrac{5(1+8\sqrt{5})}{2 \times 5}} \\
&= \sqrt{\dfrac{1+8\sqrt{5}}{2}}.
\end{align*}

Finally, we simplify the expression inside the square root:
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{\dfrac{1+8\sqrt{5}}{2}} &= \dfrac{\sqrt{1+8\sqrt{5}}}{\sqrt{2}} \\
&= \dfrac{\sqrt{1+8\sqrt{5}}}{\sqrt{2}} \times \dfrac{\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{2}} \\
&= \dfrac{\sqrt{2+16\sqrt{5}}}{2}.
\end{align*}

So the simplified form of the original expression is $\boxed{\dfrac{\sqrt{2+16\sqrt{5}}}{2}}$.

